From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sdp1804: own GPU gate/reset/idle in one genpd domain

Design 2: share the existing clock-controller mapping; one writer owns the
whole power sequence. No reset-controller or CCF gate touches these bits.
Samsung tztv-media-nike/sdp_gpu_nike/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/sdp/:
 mali_kbase_platform_sdp.c:470-494 (off/on order)
 mali_kbase_config_platform.h:101-106,128-140,150-162 (NIKEL registers/bits).
Controller base: firmware dtb0 /soc/clock-controller@00F50000 reg.
Use masked finite polling instead of Samsung's unbounded logical-AND loop.
Timeout restores the idle-request bit and leaves reset/gate unchanged.
2000 us is a software timeout policy, not a hardware timing measurement.
GPU parent/rate and mali-supply are UNBELEGT; no fabricated CCF clock.
Both DT nodes stay disabled. Compile-only; runtime/TV untested.

